in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/math/bundle

# @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian — the discrete realisation of the
# (A, H, D) triple's Dirac square at the eigenboard altitude.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# `spectral-triple.mirror` declares `type dirac_op` (D, the self-adjoint
# operator with compact resolvent) and `action eigen_d(op: dirac_op) ->
# spectrum`. It also names "the matrix form is @hash/coincidence's 5×5
# conductivity tensor." `bundle.mirror` declares `type optic` (the
# connection — what's IS-equivalent to a sheaf's restriction map in a
# chosen gauge) and the cycle-averaged-holonomy reading of κ.
#
# This shard names the discrete realisation that those declarations
# already imply:
#
#   - A `restriction` is a connection 1-form's value on one edge — the
#     parallel-transport operator the substrate calls an `optic` in
#     `bundle.mirror`. At the eigenboard altitude (cellular sheaf over
#     a finite graph) the restriction IS the matrix block.
#   - An `operator` is the assembled sheaf Laplacian Δ_F = δ*δ, the
#     discrete realisation of D² per `spectral-triple.mirror`'s
#     `dirac_op`. For an O(d)-bundle over a graph the sheaf Laplacian
#     IS the connection Laplacian (Barbero et al. 2022,
#     arXiv:2206.08702).
#   - An `eigenvalue` is one root of D's characteristic polynomial —
#     element of the `spectrum` `spectral-triple` already names. λ₀
#     (the smallest non-trivial) is the Fiedler value / algebraic
#     connectivity / spectral gap; the substrate's quantitative
#     verdict on connectivity per Bodnar et al. 2022 §2.
#
# The 18th-instance pattern: each "missing concept" the substrate
# surfaces turns out to be a name the substrate was already implicitly
# using. `operator` is the matrix shape of `dirac_op`; `restriction` is
# the in-a-gauge form of `optic`; `eigenvalue` is one element of
# `spectrum`. This shard names the discrete realisation; the abstract
# triple lives one altitude up.
#
# === Why this lives at math/, not at fate/ ===
#
# `@fate` is the tournament / inference altitude. The sheaf Laplacian
# is mathematical mechanism — it lives where the bundle, the
# spectral triple, and the principal-G structure already live.
# `@fate.minimize` (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §3.2) CONSUMES
# `lambda_zero` to read the algebraic connectivity of a tension graph;
# the consumer altitude differs from the math altitude. This shard is
# the math; `@fate.minimize` is its first consumer.
#
# === Bridge actions ===
#
# Two load-bearing actions:
#
#   sheaf_laplacian([restriction]) -> operator
#     The δ*δ assembly per Bodnar et al. 2022 §2's exact construction:
#     diagonal blocks L_{F vv} = Σ_{v ⊴ e} F_{v ⊴ e}^⊤ F_{v ⊴ e};
#     off-diagonal blocks L_{F vu} = − F_{v ⊴ e}^⊤ F_{u ⊴ e}.
#     The discrete realisation of `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `compose_a`
#     specialised to the connection-squared composition.
#
#   lambda_zero(op: operator) -> eigenvalue
#     The smallest non-trivial eigenvalue. The discrete realisation of
#     `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `eigen_d` reduced to its load-bearing
#     scalar (the spectral gap). When the bundle is connected this is
#     the Fiedler value / algebraic connectivity; when disconnected
#     λ₀ = 0 with multiplicity equal to the component count.
#
# === Floor types: substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `boot/std/number.mirror` and the audible-altitude floor in
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music/harmonic.mirror`, `ref` is the
# substrate's float-valued reference floor. An eigenvalue carries a
# `ref` because the spectral computation is realisation-layer; the
# substrate names the obligation, the FFI body discharges it.
#
# Per `bundle.mirror`'s `type optic` (the connection): the restriction
# IS a matrix block. The substrate names the connection 1-form's
# concrete realisation as `optic`; this shard names its in-a-gauge
# matrix form as `restriction`. Adjacency at the eigenboard altitude
# is integer-indexed; the index type is `u32` (matches `harmonic`'s
# `numerator: u32` precedent for small-integer cardinals).
#
# === Cellular-sheaf cardinal ===
#
# A `restriction` carries:
#   source — the source vertex index in the base graph.
#   target — the target vertex index in the base graph.
#   weight — the magnitude of the parallel-transport operator on the
#            edge (source, target). The audible-altitude floor reading
#            of the connection 1-form's strength on that edge; the full
#            matrix-block element lifts when the conductivity tensor's
#            in-a-gauge realisation pulls.
#
# This is Option-A-degraded-to-scalar in the same shape T6's
# `tension_vector` carries (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §8.1).
# The minimum that makes the discrete sheaf-Laplacian construction
# non-trivial when restriction weights vary across edges; sufficient
# for `@fate.minimize`'s ranking to become meaningful.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established object older than
# the discipline of computer science:
#
#   restriction       Leray (~1950), Godement (1958).
#   operator          Hilbert (1906), von Neumann (1932).
#   eigenvalue        Cauchy (1829), Jacobi (1846).
#   sheaf_laplacian   Hansen & Ghrist 2019, arXiv:1808.01513
#                     (extends graph-Laplacian to cellular sheaves;
#                     itself a direct descendant of Hodge 1941).
#   lambda_zero       Fiedler 1973 (`Algebraic Connectivity of Graphs`);
#                     algebraic connectivity / spectral gap.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* these so the eigenboard's
# numerical realisation has a substrate-altitude home. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md §3.2
#               (`tensor.fiedler`); docs/specs/eigenboard-representation.md
#               §"Mapping to existing references" (the 5×5 conductivity
#               tensor IS the connection matrix);
#               docs/specs/numerical-substrate-via-fortran.md §8.2 (the
#               LAPACK `dsyev` wrapper that discharges `lambda_zero`'s
#               obligation block).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (restriction, operator,
#                      and eigenvalue are each their own newtype),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (the
#                      18th-instance recognition: dirac_op, spectrum, and
#                      optic already named this).
# Related shards: boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror
#                 (the abstract (A, H, D) triple this shard's discrete
#                 realisation lives one altitude beneath),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (the
#                 principal-G tower whose connection-squared IS this
#                 shard's operator),
#                 shards/epistemologic/math/music/harmonic.mirror
#                 (the audible-register sibling under @epistemologic/math),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict; ref; the substrate floor),
#                 boot/std/number.mirror (u32 kernel primitive).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian` per the
# `@epistemologic/property/path_matches_namespace` rule.

prism @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian {
  focus sheaf_laplacian
  project sheaf_laplacian
  split sheaf_laplacian
  shift sheaf_laplacian
  settle sheaf_laplacian
}

# === The restriction carrier ===
#
# One edge of a cellular sheaf in a chosen gauge. The matrix block
# of the connection 1-form on that edge.
#
# `source` and `target` are u32 indices into the base graph's vertex
# set. `weight` carries the magnitude of the parallel-transport
# operator on that edge — the audible-altitude floor for the full
# in-a-gauge matrix block per `bundle.mirror`'s `type optic`.
#
# Identity contract: two restrictions are equal iff their (source,
# target, weight) triples are byte-equal. The realisation layer
# enforces this; the substrate names it.
#
# Audible register: a restriction is one voice-leading step between
# two adjacent fibers. The weight is the magnitude of the step; the
# direction (source → target) is the leading.
type restriction = {
  source: u32,
  target: u32,
  weight: ref,
}

# === The operator carrier ===
#
# The assembled sheaf Laplacian Δ_F = δ*δ. The discrete realisation
# of `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `type dirac_op` per Barbero et al.
# 2022 (arXiv:2206.08702): for an O(d)-bundle over a graph the sheaf
# Laplacian IS the connection Laplacian.
#
# `dimension` is the number of vertices in the base graph (= the
# operator's row/column count for the d=1 case; for higher fiber
# dimension d the operator is n*d × n*d). The substrate-altitude
# carrier names dimension; the in-a-gauge matrix block lives at the
# realisation layer.
#
# `entries` carries the operator's content-addressed representation:
# the source restrictions plus the assembly recipe. The realisation
# layer materialises the dense matrix from this representation when
# `lambda_zero` (or any future eigenmode reader) pulls.
#
# Identity contract: two operators are equal iff their (dimension,
# entries) carriers are byte-equal. The substrate names the obligation.
type operator = {
  dimension: u32,
  entries:   [restriction],
}

# === The eigenvalue carrier ===
#
# One root of the operator's characteristic polynomial. Element of
# `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `type spectrum` reduced to its scalar.
#
# `value` carries the eigenvalue as a `ref` (the substrate's
# float-valued floor; matches `harmonic.cents`'s precedent for the
# realisation-layer numerical body).
#
# `multiplicity` carries how many independent eigenvectors share this
# value — load-bearing for the connectivity reading: for the sheaf
# Laplacian on a graph with k connected components, λ₀ = 0 with
# multiplicity k (Fiedler 1973; Bodnar et al. 2022 §2).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (value, multiplicity).
type eigenvalue = {
  value:        ref,
  multiplicity: u32,
}

# === sheaf_laplacian — the δ*δ assembly ===
#
# Builds the sheaf Laplacian Δ_F from a vector of restrictions per
# Bodnar et al. 2022 §2's exact construction:
#
#   L_{F vv} = Σ_{v ⊴ e} F_{v ⊴ e}^⊤ F_{v ⊴ e}    (diagonal blocks)
#   L_{F vu} = − F_{v ⊴ e}^⊤ F_{u ⊴ e}            (off-diagonal blocks)
#
# The discrete realisation of `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `compose_a`
# specialised to the connection-squared composition.
#
# At the d=1 case (scalar fibers) the construction reduces to the
# weighted graph Laplacian L = D - W where D is the diagonal degree
# matrix and W carries the edge weights. The normalised form Δ_F =
# D^{-1/2} L D^{-1/2} is what `tensor.fiedler` reads at the
# audible-altitude floor (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §3.2).
#
# Pure; no I/O; the assembly is deterministic per IEEE-754 floating-
# point semantics on the platform.
#
# Spectrally: this IS the action that takes one element of A (the
# algebra of connections, restricted to per-edge blocks) and returns
# one element of D² (the operator's matrix form). The substrate
# names the obligation; the realisation layer (the LAPACK FFI in
# the bootstrap's `prism_core::ffi` per
# `docs/specs/numerical-substrate-via-fortran.md`) discharges it.
sheaf_laplacian(restrictions: [restriction]) -> operator { \ }

# === lambda_zero — the smallest non-trivial eigenvalue ===
#
# Returns the operator's algebraic connectivity / Fiedler value /
# spectral gap (three names; one geometric fact per
# `docs/specs/eigenboard-representation.md`'s "Mapping" section).
#
# The discrete realisation of `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `eigen_d`
# reduced to its load-bearing scalar:
#
#   - On a connected graph (single component): λ₀ is the smallest
#     strictly positive eigenvalue; the kernel of Δ_F is one-
#     dimensional per Fiedler 1973.
#   - On a disconnected graph (k components): λ₀ = 0 with
#     multiplicity k per Bodnar et al. 2022 §2; the eigenvalue
#     carrier's `multiplicity` field records this.
#   - On the trivial graph (n=0 or n=1): λ₀ = 0 with multiplicity
#     n (the additive identity on the zero-dimensional or singleton
#     section space).
#
# Audibly: λ₀ IS the lowest fundamental frequency the substrate
# tends toward when kintsugi reduces holonomy. The unison (λ₀ = 0)
# IS Lawvere's autopoietic closure — the loop closes on itself; the
# substrate has settled.
#
# `@fate.minimize` (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §3.2) reads
# `lambda_zero` on the tension graph to rank tensions by curvature;
# the SDRF curvature ranking (Topping et al. 2022, arXiv:2111.14522)
# becomes meaningful when restrictions carry non-uniform weights.
lambda_zero(op: operator) -> eigenvalue { \ }

out @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian
out restriction
out operator
out eigenvalue
out sheaf_laplacian
out lambda_zero
